#==============================================================================================
#
#   bodies - Fetch::Infrastructure::Body: a body's stream, source and length, the resource
#   header bytes for MIME type sniffing, cloning, and reading a body fully or incrementally
#
#   DESCRIPTION:
#       Port of Libraries/LibWeb/Fetch/Infrastructure/HTTP/Bodies.cpp (lines 20-217) with the
#       inline members of Bodies.h (lines 48-51). A body's stream is a Streams::ReadableStream,
#       which stays opaque until Streams are ported (phase 4): the stream operations a body
#       uses (tee, getting a reader, reading all bytes or a chunk, the stream's realm) are
#       closure stubs, and so is Fetch/BodyInit's safely_extract_body (phase 3).
#
